From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 04:25:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 15/30] doc: describe the provisional tmr() descriptor and P2MR
 wallet support

Record that tmr() and the reuse of the BIP 371 PSBT fields are placeholders
that no BIP specifies, why a single-leaf tree is refused, and what follows
from P2MR having no output type: no P2MR addresses from getnewaddress, no
P2MR change, an inactive descriptor even when imported as active, and
deriveaddresses as the way to get addresses.
